r utility share offerings were cut back in size (n6.d5).\n- **Pellham is already cutting spending.** Its 2027 plan called for capex up 18%, mostly substations and transformers. Instead it will cut transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves.\n- **Norvane is in a better position.** It plans capex up 12% and priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably. It still needs financing, but it can use debt.\n- **Debt is getting more expensive.** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp.\n\n**Caveats.** The evidence is thin: three short documents and no data series. I found no figures for Norvane's equity plans or for the total size of the funding gap, so I can't say how much of the gap debt could cover. The picture could change if equity sentiment recovers, for example through a Pellham re-launch on better terms. Until then, expect the largest buyer to scale back 2027 equipment orders, which matters for grid-equipment demand.","ttft_ms":1404,"type":"result","duration_ms":17624,"uuid":"b9fa79d1-4275-48a6-a348-56edff1912f0","ttft_stream_ms":918,"time_to_request_ms":80,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":9,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":2,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":8,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":8,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":2,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":29,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":62,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":206,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":132,"process_rss_mib_result":205,"process_anon_mib_result":124,"process_peak_rss_mib":224,"process_cpu_ms_turn":596,"process_wall_ms_turn":17623,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":104,"process_wall_ms_st